            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` function. Here's what it does:\n\n**Key features:**\n- **Concurrency limiting**: Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to ensure at most `max_concurrent` tasks run simultaneously\n- **Cleanup on interrupt**: Each task is wrapped in `async with semaphore:`, so cleanup code (try/finally, context manager exits) runs even on KeyboardInterrupt\n- **Importable**: Can be imported with `from run import run_tasks`\n\n**How it handles cleanup on interrupt:**\n- When KeyboardInterrupt occurs, asyncio cancels the pending tasks\n- Tasks already running will finish their current await point, then execute any cleanup code in finally blocks or async context manager `__aexit__` methods\n- The semaphore properly releases even when tasks are cancelled, preventing deadlocks\n\nThe function is ready to use with any async tasks you throw at it!"
